                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Humanity finally colonized the Moon. Naturally, the first thing we brought along was corporate management and quarterly profit targets.\n\nAnno 2205 lets you build beautiful futuristic cities, expand into the Arctic, and eventually establish lunar colonies. Watching your little economic empire grow is genuinely satisfying, and the visuals still look surprisingly good.\n\nUnfortunately, Ubisoft streamlined the economy so much that longtime Anno fans might wonder where half the gameplay went.\n\nTrade routes are simplified, combat feels like an unnecessary minigame, and the lack of multiplayer and meaningful competition limits replayability.\n\nHas it aged well? Visually, absolutely. The clean interface and relaxed city-building remain enjoyable, but the shallow mechanics become more noticeable compared with other Anno games.\n\nRatings:\n\nGameplay: 7/10\n\nGraphics: 8.5/10\n\nEconomy & Management: 6.5/10\n\nReplayability: 6/10\n\nEnjoyment: 7/10\n\nA gorgeous, accessible city-builder that's enjoyable without being particularly challenging. Great for casual players, less impressive for strategy veterans.\n\nOverall: 7/10 | Recommended, preferably on sale.",
